WEBVTT

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:02.940
Souta-kun.

00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:04.940
Souta-kun.

00:00:06.090 --> 00:00:07.290
Souta-kun.

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:11.050
Good morning,

00:00:11.050 --> 00:00:11.940
Souta-kun.

00:00:12.980 --> 00:00:14.160
Good morning...

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:18.000
Huh?! Why are you in my room?!

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:19.280
I just walked in.

00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:20.870
Why all the noise...

00:00:21.470 --> 00:00:23.870
We just woke up and you're trying 
to get down and dirty already?!

00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:25.850
No, no.

00:00:25.850 --> 00:00:27.470
This is what they do in France.

00:00:27.470 --> 00:00:28.500
You're French?!

00:00:28.860 --> 00:00:31.210
How did you unlock the door, anyway?

00:00:31.210 --> 00:00:34.180
I borrowed the spare key 
from Kikuno-senpai.

00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:37.280
Why does Okiku-nee have 
the spare key to my room?

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:38.870
She said that sisters can 
do that sort of thing.

00:00:38.870 --> 00:00:39.970
What the hell?!

00:00:40.730 --> 00:00:42.730
I heard that men really like it

00:00:42.730 --> 00:00:45.480
when girls wake them up in the morning.

00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:47.990
You should wake him up with me

00:00:47.990 --> 00:00:50.090
so he'll be really happy!

00:00:50.790 --> 00:00:54.740
You're triggering all the 
fun "events," aren't you, Souta?

00:00:55.070 --> 00:00:57.580
Why are you complaining about me?

00:00:57.850 --> 00:00:58.580
Huh?

00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:14.250
Oh, good morning, each and every one.

00:01:17.020 --> 00:01:19.170
Th-This had to happen.

00:01:19.170 --> 00:01:22.140
This is how men strengthen 
their friendships.

00:01:22.380 --> 00:01:23.350
You perv.

00:01:23.350 --> 00:01:24.730
Perv!

00:01:24.730 --> 00:01:25.810
That's not it!

00:01:25.810 --> 00:01:27.950
Why are you in my room, Megumu?!

00:01:28.290 --> 00:01:30.980
I was pretty sure I went to 
the bathroom last night...

00:01:31.530 --> 00:01:32.600
Oh, yeah!

00:01:32.600 --> 00:01:35.260
I was half asleep, so Kikuno-senpai

00:01:35.260 --> 00:01:37.360
helped me back to my room.

00:01:37.360 --> 00:01:39.370
Behind all great mysteries, 
there is a sister.

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:41.470
Sou-kun, breakfast's ready.

00:01:41.470 --> 00:01:42.770
Hm?

00:01:43.070 --> 00:01:46.720
Sou-kun's surrounded by women 
so early in the morning.

00:01:46.720 --> 00:01:47.790
Your sister's so proud!

00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:50.990
She planned all of it.

00:01:50.990 --> 00:01:53.870
I-I'm a guy, though...

00:01:53.870 --> 00:01:57.800
Kikuno-senpai will do anything 
to make sure Souta is happy!

00:01:57.800 --> 00:01:59.300
She's ruthless!

00:02:11.330 --> 00:02:13.320
Wh-What was that?

00:02:19.780 --> 00:02:24.290
<b>If Her Flag Breaks</b>

00:03:44.030 --> 00:03:47.990
<b>Flag 3</b>

00:03:44.030 --> 00:03:47.990
<b>Leave it to Me,
We Have a 99.9% Chance We're Going to Win This Athletic Meet</b>

00:03:47.990 --> 00:03:48.790
<b>Mahougasawa Group</b>

00:03:50.600 --> 00:03:52.460
What's this?

00:04:06.180 --> 00:04:08.430
A-A girl?

00:04:11.360 --> 00:04:14.690
Operation system check: OK.

00:04:14.950 --> 00:04:18.040
Each part operation check: OK.

00:04:18.500 --> 00:04:20.280
The main system start.

00:04:20.740 --> 00:04:22.110
Hello world.

00:04:23.420 --> 00:04:25.880
She's speaking English! She's robot!

00:04:25.880 --> 00:04:28.200
I guess Akane thinks all the 
robots come from America.

00:04:28.790 --> 00:04:29.940
Nice to meet you.

00:04:30.410 --> 00:04:33.970
I have been assigned to the 
Quest Dorm cluster as of today.

00:04:33.970 --> 00:04:35.710
My name is Ninjabayashi Ruri.

00:04:35.710 --> 00:04:38.230
She's speaking Japanese! 
She's a robot!

00:04:38.230 --> 00:04:39.840
So the language doesn't even matter!

00:04:40.240 --> 00:04:41.710
It's a pleasure—

00:04:44.330 --> 00:04:46.220
—to meet you all.

00:04:50.980 --> 00:04:52.300
I'm sorry about that.

00:04:52.300 --> 00:04:54.030
There was a slight error 
in my connections

00:04:54.030 --> 00:04:56.850
due to the shock of falling 
in that container.

00:04:57.150 --> 00:04:58.600
Wrong way.

00:04:59.620 --> 00:05:00.810
To continue,

00:05:01.110 --> 00:05:04.040
I was dispatched from 
Mahougasawa Electronics

00:05:04.340 --> 00:05:07.740
to help Akane-ojousama with her life here.

00:05:07.960 --> 00:05:09.520
<i>She pretended like nothing happened...</i>

00:05:09.520 --> 00:05:12.250
Mahougasawa Electronics?

00:05:12.250 --> 00:05:13.750
So she's related to 
Akane-chan's family?

00:05:14.120 --> 00:05:15.940
Just call me Akane.

00:05:15.940 --> 00:05:18.330
You don't have to add the "ojousama."

00:05:18.780 --> 00:05:22.420
In order to abbreviate your name, 
I need to be in administrator mode.

00:05:22.820 --> 00:05:26.220
Would you like to enter your password 
and change me to administrator mode?

00:05:26.490 --> 00:05:28.220
Yes or no.

00:05:28.480 --> 00:05:30.730
I don't know the password!

00:05:30.730 --> 00:05:32.730
Password is incorrect.

00:05:32.730 --> 00:05:34.220
Would you like to enter it again?

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:36.230
Yes or no.

00:05:36.230 --> 00:05:38.740
I don't know the password!

00:05:38.740 --> 00:05:41.230
Would you like to enter it again?

00:05:39.860 --> 00:05:41.230
This is going to go on forever!

00:05:42.630 --> 00:05:45.990
Now Sou-kun has more girls in his life.

00:05:46.420 --> 00:05:48.490
Your sister won't know 
what to do with herself.

00:05:48.490 --> 00:05:52.080
Sou-kun, remember to restrain 
yourself!  You can't just jump at the girls.

00:05:52.310 --> 00:05:54.900
I'm sure that's why she was sent here.

00:05:55.200 --> 00:05:58.660
The daughter of the 
Mahougasawa family is

00:05:58.660 --> 00:06:01.050
staying here in a dorm with 
men, albeit just one.

00:06:03.410 --> 00:06:05.250
Yeah, I can see why they'd worry about

00:06:05.250 --> 00:06:08.720
having her live with a guy who acted 
like he just rode into her life.

00:06:08.970 --> 00:06:11.560
You may have just rode in,

00:06:11.560 --> 00:06:14.570
but it was on a thoroughbred!

00:06:14.570 --> 00:06:16.180
I still just rode in, though.

00:06:16.480 --> 00:06:19.120
But you're acting like you'll 
be sent for slaughter.

00:06:19.120 --> 00:06:20.730
That was a strangely real example.

00:06:21.060 --> 00:06:25.480
Have I been accepted into this cluster?

00:06:25.890 --> 00:06:28.220
Yes! We'd be glad to have you!

00:06:28.220 --> 00:06:29.570
"Right," right?

00:06:29.570 --> 00:06:30.910
I don't see the problem.

00:06:30.910 --> 00:06:33.480
The more the merrier.

00:06:33.480 --> 00:06:35.490
Men are ready for anything!

00:06:36.240 --> 00:06:37.500
Well, if everyone insists...

00:06:39.070 --> 00:06:40.830
I welcome you, Ruri.

00:06:43.110 --> 00:06:44.520
Ruri-chan is blushing!

00:06:44.520 --> 00:06:46.450
Just like a real human!

00:06:46.750 --> 00:06:47.820
I'm not blushing.

00:06:47.820 --> 00:06:49.780
Really? You look like—

00:06:49.780 --> 00:06:50.800
I'm not.

00:06:51.100 --> 00:06:55.100
You couldn't have gotten 
Ruri's flag, too, did you?

00:06:55.100 --> 00:06:57.950
I don't think robots have flags...

00:06:57.950 --> 00:06:59.560
I think, anyway.

00:06:59.800 --> 00:07:00.870
Oh, no.

00:07:00.870 --> 00:07:02.200
We have to hurry.

00:07:02.200 --> 00:07:04.480
We're going to be late 
if we don't leave soon.

00:07:04.730 --> 00:07:07.390
That was quite the 
commotion this morning.

00:07:07.390 --> 00:07:09.730
Nanami-chan, that's my bag.

00:07:09.730 --> 00:07:13.170
Sou-kun, this is the perfect chance 
for me to carry you on my back.

00:07:13.170 --> 00:07:15.170
I think I'll be fine by myself.

00:07:16.450 --> 00:07:19.390
Anyway, Ruri-chan, could you 
watch the house for us—

00:07:20.160 --> 00:07:21.740
Let's get going.

00:07:21.740 --> 00:07:24.140
As you can see, I'm fully functional.

00:07:25.050 --> 00:07:29.940
<i>All right, let's play our lunch show's first number!</i>

00:07:33.080 --> 00:07:35.100
That's some nice electricity you're using.

00:07:35.500 --> 00:07:38.060
You sure got settled in 
quickly your first day.

00:07:38.060 --> 00:07:39.660
You're a good girl,

00:07:39.660 --> 00:07:42.520
so I'm glad you got along 
with everyone in class.

00:07:42.520 --> 00:07:45.110
I think someone here should follow Ruri's lead

00:07:45.110 --> 00:07:47.300
and become a bit better themselves.

00:07:47.300 --> 00:07:49.110
Sorry I'm a bad apple.

00:07:49.110 --> 00:07:50.650
What are you saying?

00:07:50.650 --> 00:07:52.150
You're nice, Souta-kun!

00:07:52.450 --> 00:07:54.230
Don't berate yourself, Sou-kun!

00:07:54.230 --> 00:07:56.990
I'll wash your hair when 
we take a bath later!

00:07:56.990 --> 00:08:00.290
If you're a bad apple, 
I'll be a bad apple, too!

00:08:00.690 --> 00:08:03.790
Must be nice getting 
so much love every day.

00:08:05.170 --> 00:08:06.660
<i>Sorry to interrupt the song,</i>

00:08:06.660 --> 00:08:09.570
<i>but we have an announcement 
from Seiteikouji Mimori,</i>

00:08:09.570 --> 00:08:10.800
<i>the student council president.</i>

00:08:11.080 --> 00:08:15.200
<i>My beloved students, Hatagaya Academy!</i>

00:08:12.800 --> 00:08:20.560
<b>Student Council President</b>

00:08:15.200 --> 00:08:17.510
<i>By the way "Hatagaya Academy" is an</i>

00:08:17.510 --> 00:08:20.560
<i>original earth-shattering 
greeting that I invented.</i>

00:08:20.830 --> 00:08:21.740
What?

00:08:22.060 --> 00:08:24.520
<i>Anyway, it's almost time 
for our school track meet,</i>

00:08:24.520 --> 00:08:26.940
<i>and I want to scale it up this year.</i>

00:08:26.940 --> 00:08:29.940
<b>Track Meet Week</b>

00:08:27.820 --> 00:08:30.050
<i>I'm calling it the Track Meet Week.</i>

00:08:30.370 --> 00:08:33.830
<i>It's a week-long event that 
has all different types of</i>

00:08:33.830 --> 00:08:35.810
<i>events that take place from 
morning all the way through the night.</i>

00:08:35.810 --> 00:08:39.100
<i>It's a huge, non-stop event.</i>

00:08:39.400 --> 00:08:41.870
<i>The students will spend 
a week dueling it out,</i>

00:08:41.870 --> 00:08:45.790
<i>and the best team will 
be designated MVP!</i>

00:08:46.270 --> 00:08:47.780
This is great!

00:08:47.780 --> 00:08:49.290
It sounds so fun!

00:08:49.560 --> 00:08:52.580
I'll be able to see Sou-kun 
kicking butt for a week!

00:08:52.580 --> 00:08:53.840
I'm so happy!

00:08:53.840 --> 00:08:55.400
I know, right?

00:08:55.400 --> 00:08:57.610
What events are you guys doing?

00:08:57.610 --> 00:08:59.990
I'm going to do the three-legged 
race with Sou-kun!

00:08:59.990 --> 00:09:01.240
No, that's no fair!

00:09:01.240 --> 00:09:02.680
I want to do it, too.

00:09:02.680 --> 00:09:03.640
Me, too! Me, too!

00:09:03.930 --> 00:09:06.390
You guys always look like 
you're having so much fun.

00:09:07.370 --> 00:09:10.150
<i>Man, with all of this going on...</i>

00:09:15.280 --> 00:09:17.740
<i>...I really don't have 
time to think about much.</i>

00:09:20.430 --> 00:09:23.350
We've discussed things, 
and we've decided to wrap you up,

00:09:23.350 --> 00:09:26.450
put Megu-chan on top of you, and then 
Kikuno-senpai and I will drag you

00:09:26.450 --> 00:09:29.080
while we do the three-legged 
race together.

00:09:29.080 --> 00:09:30.460
Is that some kind of torture?

00:09:30.460 --> 00:09:33.090
They forgot what they were 
after in the beginning.

00:09:33.090 --> 00:09:35.470
Hey. I was looking for you guys.

00:09:35.890 --> 00:09:38.430
I'm glad to see you all 
getting along again today.

00:09:38.430 --> 00:09:40.400
Yes, we're very grateful for

00:09:40.400 --> 00:09:42.710
your having fixed the Quest Dorm.

00:09:42.710 --> 00:09:45.430
Though, granny was the one 
that helped the most.

00:09:45.700 --> 00:09:47.350
Right. So anyway,

00:09:47.350 --> 00:09:49.810
About Quest Dorm...

00:09:50.540 --> 00:09:52.980
Sorry. You might get shut down after all.

00:09:54.570 --> 00:09:56.550
What?!

00:10:04.390 --> 00:10:05.660
Student Council President—

00:10:05.660 --> 00:10:07.480
I mean, our tentative chairwoman.

00:10:07.480 --> 00:10:11.230
Apparently this Quest Dorm 
only has five residents.

00:10:11.230 --> 00:10:13.670
It doesn't make sense to run this 
facility with so few people.

00:10:13.900 --> 00:10:16.610
It's also co-ed.

00:10:16.610 --> 00:10:18.120
I'm so jealous—

00:10:18.440 --> 00:10:19.680
I mean this is untenable!

00:10:23.540 --> 00:10:24.640
Don't cry!

00:10:24.640 --> 00:10:27.180
We weren't trying to 
give you a hard time.

00:10:27.180 --> 00:10:29.440
We were just discussing 
the situation...

00:10:30.170 --> 00:10:31.860
I was just faking it.

00:10:32.110 --> 00:10:33.660
Why you...

00:10:33.660 --> 00:10:36.910
It's sad that you're taking your 
problems out on someone else,

00:10:36.910 --> 00:10:39.360
just because you didn't have 
fun while you were younger.

00:10:39.360 --> 00:10:41.430
Y-You shouldn't have said that!

00:10:41.430 --> 00:10:45.430
It's a co-ed dorm because we 
haphazardly decided to let him

00:10:45.430 --> 00:10:47.750
transfer in when all the male 
dorms were already full.

00:10:48.500 --> 00:10:52.500
Also, the members of the 
Quest Dorm have strong bonds

00:10:52.500 --> 00:10:56.000
and trust one another, 
much more than any other club or dorm.

00:10:56.740 --> 00:10:59.130
It would be sheer foolishness 
to attempt to dismantle that.

00:10:59.380 --> 00:11:00.970
There's not a single good 
that would come from it.

00:11:04.040 --> 00:11:09.520
I wouldn't be surprised if they 
got MVP in the school meet.

00:11:10.090 --> 00:11:11.350
You think so?!

00:11:11.350 --> 00:11:15.550
No co-ed team has ever made MVP!

00:11:15.550 --> 00:11:16.370
So envious!

00:11:16.370 --> 00:11:19.530
There'll be too much flirting going on
for them to get anywhere!

00:11:19.930 --> 00:11:21.100
I see.

00:11:21.400 --> 00:11:24.410
So if they don't make MVP, 
we shut down Quest Dorm.

00:11:24.410 --> 00:11:27.290
We expel Hatate-kun from our school.

00:11:28.290 --> 00:11:30.710
Sure. I'll accept those conditions.

00:11:31.740 --> 00:11:34.210
We didn't say anything like that...

00:11:34.210 --> 00:11:37.330
I'll show you the ultimate team!

00:11:39.100 --> 00:11:40.920
This is your fault!

00:11:40.920 --> 00:11:44.850
Now, let's show those crazy adults your—

00:11:48.620 --> 00:11:52.480
What do you mean Sou-kun 
might get expelled?!

00:11:52.480 --> 00:11:54.130
I-I-It'll be fine.

00:11:54.130 --> 00:11:56.860
I-I-I have a plan.

00:11:56.860 --> 00:12:00.450
Okiku-nee, I think that's enough, don't you?

00:12:00.450 --> 00:12:02.360
Sou-kun, you're so kind.

00:12:02.730 --> 00:12:05.790
Your sister's so happy to see you've 
grown up to be such a great kid.

00:12:05.790 --> 00:12:07.330
I was so scared!

00:12:08.640 --> 00:12:10.830
You guys don't need to join them.

00:12:11.080 --> 00:12:12.830
Well, I was just pretending to cry.

00:12:13.250 --> 00:12:15.790
I've verified that your tear 
ducts are fully dilated.

00:12:15.790 --> 00:12:17.450
In addition, there seems 
to be some moisture

00:12:17.450 --> 00:12:19.420
that was expelled from the 
lower part of your body.

00:12:20.000 --> 00:12:22.710
I didn't wet myself!

00:12:23.590 --> 00:12:25.430
A-Anyway, you know how it is.

00:12:25.430 --> 00:12:29.210
I've got you some excellent 
help for the meet,

00:12:29.210 --> 00:12:30.600
so cut me some slack.

00:12:30.820 --> 00:12:32.140
Help?

00:12:32.140 --> 00:12:34.400
Someone with excellent leadership skills

00:12:34.400 --> 00:12:36.890
that will help you all become MVPs.

00:12:37.190 --> 00:12:38.720
Anyway, I'm going to 
stop by the restroom—

00:12:39.020 --> 00:12:40.650
I mean the student council's office.

00:12:44.240 --> 00:12:45.420
It'll be okay!

00:12:45.420 --> 00:12:49.350
When you get expelled, I'll go with you!

00:12:49.350 --> 00:12:52.360
I won't leave you alone, either.

00:12:52.360 --> 00:12:55.660
We'll ride the harsh seas 
of society together as men.

00:12:56.000 --> 00:12:58.420
You're expecting me to get expelled, huh?

00:12:58.760 --> 00:13:01.120
I wonder who the help's gonna be.

00:13:01.120 --> 00:13:03.610
Maybe another dorm mate!

00:13:04.550 --> 00:13:08.420
What if it's a scary guy... Huh, Souta-kun?

00:13:10.160 --> 00:13:12.890
Discipline... is needed!

00:13:19.060 --> 00:13:22.060
I'm in class 2-F, Eiyuuzaki Rin.

00:13:22.360 --> 00:13:24.820
I will be entering 
Quest Dorm in order to

00:13:24.820 --> 00:13:26.660
make sure you become MVPs.

00:13:27.020 --> 00:13:30.250
I normally wouldn't want to 
work for some weakling who

00:13:30.250 --> 00:13:32.000
gets pushed around by a bunch of girls.

00:13:32.000 --> 00:13:33.540
However, I owe the president a favor.

00:13:34.140 --> 00:13:36.780
I do not wish to be here, but I will 
do the job to the best of my ability.

00:13:37.760 --> 00:13:40.540
<i>Your typical "hates men" flag...</i>

00:13:40.540 --> 00:13:44.750
Now, now, Rin-chan, 
you'll scare the kids if you're too angry.

00:13:44.750 --> 00:13:47.170
Okiku. I don't even understand 
why you're here.

00:13:47.170 --> 00:13:49.410
What's the point of being 
around this random guy?

00:13:49.410 --> 00:13:52.310
I know him, so he's not random.

00:13:52.310 --> 00:13:53.510
He's random.

00:13:55.820 --> 00:13:58.560
Rin-chan was in my class last year.

00:13:58.560 --> 00:14:01.730
We talked to each other, 
even while I was overseas.

00:14:02.720 --> 00:14:06.730
You only ever talked about your neighbors
and brother in your letters.

00:14:06.730 --> 00:14:08.390
Sou-kun this, and Sou-kun that...

00:14:09.950 --> 00:14:10.990
Wait a second...

00:14:11.310 --> 00:14:12.740
That's Sou-kun?!

00:14:13.600 --> 00:14:14.580
That's right.

00:14:15.000 --> 00:14:16.380
So you were able to see him again?

00:14:16.380 --> 00:14:17.730
I'm glad for you.

00:14:18.030 --> 00:14:19.910
But that doesn't mean I'm going to hold back!

00:14:19.910 --> 00:14:22.060
Since you're the only man here,

00:14:22.060 --> 00:14:23.960
I'm going to work you as hard as I can!

00:14:24.770 --> 00:14:27.010
Uh, well, Megumu is male, too...

00:14:27.290 --> 00:14:29.870
Oh, yeah. Megu-chan was here, too.

00:14:29.870 --> 00:14:32.260
I nearly forgot myself.

00:14:32.670 --> 00:14:36.310
Amending data: 
rewriting gender from female to male.

00:14:37.070 --> 00:14:38.160
Male?

00:14:38.160 --> 00:14:39.940
He's cuter than I am.

00:14:40.240 --> 00:14:41.560
Whatever!

00:14:41.560 --> 00:14:45.570
Anyway, I'm just here to help you get MVP!

00:14:46.110 --> 00:14:47.190
Understood?!

00:14:48.290 --> 00:14:49.700
Rise!

00:14:50.390 --> 00:14:51.890
What's going on...

00:14:52.240 --> 00:14:54.090
It's not even six yet.

00:14:54.410 --> 00:14:57.940
You're trying to become 
MVPs looking like that?

00:14:57.940 --> 00:14:58.660
Straighten yourselves up!

00:14:58.920 --> 00:15:00.850
Why are we up so early?

00:15:00.850 --> 00:15:02.700
Isn't it obvious? We train.

00:15:03.130 --> 00:15:05.680
So what happened to Okiku and Ruri?

00:15:05.680 --> 00:15:07.570
Okiku-nee only wakes 
up when she wants to,

00:15:07.570 --> 00:15:09.680
regardless of what's going on.

00:15:09.680 --> 00:15:11.580
Oh, yeah, I remember that.

00:15:11.580 --> 00:15:12.930
We need to at least get Ruri out here.

00:15:14.430 --> 00:15:17.120
I am currently operating in sleep mode.

00:15:17.120 --> 00:15:19.560
There are twenty minutes remaining 
before I am finished charging.

00:15:19.560 --> 00:15:22.480
After which, it will take five 
minutes for a system refresh.

00:15:22.480 --> 00:15:25.070
Please wait twenty-five minutes 
until I am operational.

00:15:25.070 --> 00:15:27.050
R-Right.

00:15:28.030 --> 00:15:30.850
You're not very good with electronics?

00:15:30.850 --> 00:15:32.300
Th-That was rude.

00:15:32.300 --> 00:15:33.610
I'm great with them!

00:15:33.610 --> 00:15:36.090
I can type texts with one hand!

00:15:36.090 --> 00:15:37.200
This is also water resistant.

00:15:37.200 --> 00:15:38.090
Pretty cool, right?

00:15:38.090 --> 00:15:39.370
<i>Strangely cute.</i>

00:15:39.370 --> 00:15:41.750
Anyway, we don't have time!

00:15:41.750 --> 00:15:43.210
We need to start training.

00:15:43.210 --> 00:15:44.960
Hurry up and change!

00:15:45.180 --> 00:15:46.870
Run faster! Faster!

00:15:48.170 --> 00:15:50.180
We're working those biceps.

00:15:51.510 --> 00:15:53.450
Now, pull ups...

00:15:54.970 --> 00:15:56.540
Become the bunny!

00:16:01.520 --> 00:16:03.730
What an exhausting day...

00:16:03.990 --> 00:16:06.460
Hm? Where's Sou-kun and Rin-chan?

00:16:06.460 --> 00:16:09.210
Rin-senpai said she was 
going for another run,

00:16:09.210 --> 00:16:11.070
and dragged Souta along with her.

00:16:11.070 --> 00:16:13.990
Rin-senpai's a Spartan.

00:16:19.130 --> 00:16:20.000
Let me take a short break.

00:16:20.490 --> 00:16:22.430
You're tired already?

00:16:22.730 --> 00:16:24.750
Guys are useless.

00:16:24.750 --> 00:16:27.660
You're pretty strict.

00:16:28.390 --> 00:16:30.630
I'm trying pretty hard.

00:16:31.660 --> 00:16:34.860
Trying pretty hard so you can 
live surrounded by women?

00:16:35.160 --> 00:16:36.140
Ridiculous drivel.

00:16:36.500 --> 00:16:39.430
Oh, no! For some reason, Megu-chan's...

00:16:39.690 --> 00:16:45.230
I don't know why Okiku and the others 
are working so hard for you.

00:16:45.740 --> 00:16:46.960
Neither do I.

00:16:47.360 --> 00:16:49.840
Why are you acting like this doesn't 
have anything to do with you?

00:16:49.840 --> 00:16:52.490
The dorm will be shut down 
and you'll be kicked out.

00:16:52.940 --> 00:16:56.430
Yeah, I know everyone's 
working hard for me.

00:16:56.750 --> 00:16:59.180
Yet everything feels so surreal.

00:16:59.660 --> 00:17:02.040
Maybe it's because I've 
been alone for so long.

00:17:04.520 --> 00:17:07.120
Nothing but trivialities 
and complaints from you.

00:17:07.120 --> 00:17:08.790
You're a pathetic man.

00:17:09.160 --> 00:17:13.010
What type of a guy do you like, anyway?

00:17:13.430 --> 00:17:15.300
Isn't that obvious?

00:17:15.720 --> 00:17:20.090
I wonder if Rin-senpai has always 
been hard on men like that?

00:17:20.090 --> 00:17:24.020
There was a boy she was really 
close to when she was younger.

00:17:24.400 --> 00:17:26.130
I think his name was...

00:17:26.560 --> 00:17:28.250
His name was Souda.

00:17:28.540 --> 00:17:32.310
He's the only man I like in the entire world.

00:17:34.490 --> 00:17:36.820
You're going to become my lackey today.

00:17:37.060 --> 00:17:38.300
Not happening.

00:17:39.070 --> 00:17:41.360
You're a wimp, Souda!

00:17:41.360 --> 00:17:43.010
Don't call me Souda!

00:17:44.220 --> 00:17:47.820
Every boy knew I was better than them,

00:17:47.820 --> 00:17:52.260
and Souda was the only one
who'd try to face me head-on.

00:17:52.680 --> 00:17:55.330
And eventually we

00:17:55.330 --> 00:17:57.430
did everything together.

00:18:00.480 --> 00:18:02.310
I felt like I could do anything

00:18:02.560 --> 00:18:04.810
with him by my side.

00:18:06.850 --> 00:18:08.560
Souda!

00:18:14.310 --> 00:18:15.460
Souda!

00:18:16.100 --> 00:18:19.830
Souda!

00:18:20.330 --> 00:18:22.030
His name was Souda.

00:18:23.260 --> 00:18:25.220
He will be forever my best friend.

00:18:25.800 --> 00:18:26.800
Listen,

00:18:26.800 --> 00:18:30.640
there are some men in this world you 
could never dream of living up to.

00:18:31.230 --> 00:18:32.250
That's a coincidence.

00:18:32.680 --> 00:18:35.300
I used to be called 
Souda a long time ago.

00:18:36.380 --> 00:18:38.410
It's a small world after all.

00:18:39.320 --> 00:18:41.720
I think I'll tell him about you.

00:18:41.720 --> 00:18:45.810
We moved apart, but I still text him.

00:18:46.860 --> 00:18:48.210
You've got mail.

00:18:51.600 --> 00:18:54.390
I was just talking about you, Souda.

00:18:54.710 --> 00:18:57.370
It got me to thinking about our past.

00:18:57.960 --> 00:18:59.820
I miss you.

00:19:00.060 --> 00:19:00.750
Huh?

00:19:01.630 --> 00:19:03.260
Rin...kun?

00:19:03.560 --> 00:19:05.400
Sou...da?

00:19:07.750 --> 00:19:09.680
You were just
a kid bully!

00:19:09.680 --> 00:19:10.920
When did you start 
dressing like a girl?!

00:19:10.920 --> 00:19:12.290
I was always a girl!

00:19:12.290 --> 00:19:14.400
And you, you used to be lively 
and straight-forward...

00:19:14.400 --> 00:19:17.970
Why are you all pessimistic, 
like you've given up on life?!

00:19:26.390 --> 00:19:27.520
Are you okay?

00:19:29.770 --> 00:19:30.720
No fair...

00:19:30.720 --> 00:19:31.520
Huh?

00:19:31.520 --> 00:19:34.850
This sucks! Why are you 
like this only now?

00:19:34.850 --> 00:19:37.170
You keep getting more manly...

00:19:38.150 --> 00:19:39.740
Huh? Rin-kun...

00:19:40.320 --> 00:19:43.010
You hate me now, don't you?

00:19:43.010 --> 00:19:44.660
I don't...

00:19:44.660 --> 00:19:45.710
Of course you do!

00:19:45.710 --> 00:19:49.080
I kept saying all those 
bad things about you...

00:19:49.080 --> 00:19:50.910
I was an insufferable woman.

00:19:51.510 --> 00:19:53.670
I'm sorry. I'm sorry. 
I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

00:19:53.670 --> 00:19:55.710
<i>This is what happens when a</i>

00:19:55.710 --> 00:19:57.990
<i>pathological love 
drives someone to insane actions...</i>

00:19:58.420 --> 00:19:59.920
<i>The "yandere" flag...</i>

00:20:00.220 --> 00:20:02.680
<i>I don't want to get involved, but...</i>

00:20:02.680 --> 00:20:04.530
I-It's okay.

00:20:04.530 --> 00:20:07.640
My friendship with you wouldn't end 
just because of something like this.

00:20:10.090 --> 00:20:11.310
Really?

00:20:11.310 --> 00:20:13.150
Yeah, of course.

00:20:14.650 --> 00:20:16.140
Yeah, you're right.

00:20:16.140 --> 00:20:18.120
You're Souda!

00:20:19.340 --> 00:20:21.760
Souda! Souda!

00:20:20.240 --> 00:20:20.900
Huh?

00:20:22.200 --> 00:20:25.160
<i>The "conquest complete" flag?!</i>

00:20:26.410 --> 00:20:28.560
<i>Rin-kun, why...</i>

00:20:29.170 --> 00:20:31.260
<i>Why are you so easy...</i>

00:20:31.970 --> 00:20:36.090
So Sou-kun was Rin-chan's
childhood friend, Souda.

00:20:36.090 --> 00:20:39.000
Running into a childhood friend. 
It's like fate!

00:20:39.000 --> 00:20:41.650
Why didn't you two notice?

00:20:41.650 --> 00:20:43.760
So what happened?

00:20:43.760 --> 00:20:47.640
Well, he was embarrassed about
being called Souda and all.

00:20:47.640 --> 00:20:50.060
So I've been calling him Souta now.

00:20:51.670 --> 00:20:53.490
It looks like you're talking about 
the scene that just happened.

00:20:53.490 --> 00:20:54.740
I've recorded it.

00:20:54.740 --> 00:20:56.100
Would you like me to replay it?

00:20:56.100 --> 00:20:57.400
Yes or no.

00:20:57.400 --> 00:20:58.840
No! No!

00:20:58.840 --> 00:21:01.310
Well, could you give the file to me—

00:21:01.310 --> 00:21:02.430
I've deleted it.

00:21:08.320 --> 00:21:09.910
Is everyone ready?!

00:21:09.910 --> 00:21:10.840
Yes.

00:21:11.660 --> 00:21:14.760
The fate of Souta and Quest Dorm depends on this battle.

00:21:14.760 --> 00:21:16.420
We cannot lose!

00:21:16.650 --> 00:21:17.540
Right!

00:21:17.540 --> 00:21:18.670
Yeppers.

00:21:18.890 --> 00:21:19.800
Of course!

00:21:20.200 --> 00:21:21.300
I'd imagine so.

00:21:21.600 --> 00:21:22.550
Roger that.

00:21:22.570 --> 00:21:25.770
Now, it's time for track meet week!

00:21:25.770 --> 00:21:26.550
Let's go!

00:21:26.970 --> 00:21:28.860
Right!

00:23:10.820 --> 00:23:12.340
Roar! Gawo!

00:23:12.340 --> 00:23:14.970
Why have a school track meet for a week?

00:23:14.970 --> 00:23:16.530
How about we make it an hour instead?

00:23:16.530 --> 00:23:18.370
We might as well just have PE, then!

00:23:18.370 --> 00:23:23.420
The longer it is, 
the more Souta can cheer me on!

00:23:23.420 --> 00:23:28.800
Hey, Souta. Don't stare at 
me with such passion...

00:23:28.800 --> 00:23:32.560
I can't even see flags, 
and I can tell how easy hers is.

00:23:32.010 --> 00:23:35.010
<b>Flag 4</b>

00:23:32.010 --> 00:23:35.010
<b>We're Almost to the Goal. The Track Meet'll End Just Fine.</b>

00:23:32.860 --> 00:23:34.490
Roar! Gawo!

00:23:35.010 --> 00:23:40.010
<b>Will you watch next time? (Yes/Yes)</b>

00:23:35.010 --> 00:23:40.010
<b>If Her Flag Breaks</b>

00:23:35.010 --> 00:23:40.010
Illustration: Kuroyuki Kazuki
